   "title": "How to use",
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "H3 Cutscene: one shot (Blender previs -> MiniMax H3)\n1) Render the previs with cutscene/tools/render_review.py. Load shots_gray/Sxx.mp4 (scaled to 704x384) into <Video 1>.\n2) Paint the first frame of the shot (cutscene/tools/paint_h3image.py) and load it into First frame. H3 pins it.\n3) Load the character sheet into <Picture 1> and write the prompt (the example is the Harbor shot S03).\n4) length = the shot's frames (17n+5, 124 = 5.2 s). Run.\ncutscene/tools/h3_shot.py does 1) to 4) from cutscene.json and h3.json, one command per shot."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
